      "number": 3,
      "pali": "Ajjhattātītayadaniccasutta ",
      "english": "The Interior and What’s Impermanent in the Past "
    },
    {
      "number": 4,
      "pali": "“Cakkhu, bhikkhave, aniccaṁ atītaṁ. ",
      "english": "“Mendicants, in the past the eye, ear, nose, tongue, body, and mind were impermanent. "
    },
    {
      "number": 5,
      "pali": "Yadaniccaṁ, taṁ dukkhaṁ. ",
      "english": "What’s impermanent is suffering. "
    },
    {
      "number": 6,
      "pali": "Yaṁ dukkhaṁ, tadanattā. ",
      "english": "What’s suffering is not-self. "
    },
    {
      "number": 7,
      "pali": "Yadanattā, taṁ ‘netaṁ mama, nesohamasmi, na meso attā’ti evametaṁ yathābhūtaṁ sammappaññāya daṭṭhabbaṁ …pe… ",
      "english": "And what’s not-self should be truly seen with right understanding like this: ‘This is not mine, I am not this, this is not my self.’ …” "
    },
